Patient presents with chronic lower back pain that has persisted for over 6 months. Pain is described as dull and aching, rated 7/10 on the pain scale. Pain radiates down the left leg. Patient has tried over-the-counter NSAIDs with minimal relief. Physical therapy was attempted for 4 weeks with no significant improvement. MRI shows L4-L5 disc herniation with nerve root compression. Patient is requesting referral to pain management specialist for epidural steroid injections.
